      <main id="content"><article class="proof-reader" data-authored-declaration="AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.FunctionalInequalities.GaussianCompactEntropy.compact_count_gaussian_entropy_limits"><div class="eyebrow">Samplinglib mathematical lesson</div><h1>Actual compact Gaussian observer and homogeneous entropy limits</h1><p><code>AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.FunctionalInequalities.GaussianCompactEntropy.compact_count_gaussian_entropy_limits</code> · theorem · <a href="index.html">Teaching coverage</a></p><section class="reader-first-pass" aria-label="First reading"><div class="reader-first-pass-label">Read this first</div><h2>Mathematical statement</h2><p class="reader-claim">For every real C2 function f with compact support, the actual variance-one centered Gaussian integrates f squared, f squared times log(f squared), and the square of its real derivative. Each actual normalized Bool counting measure integrates those same functions of the signed sum divided by sqrt(N), including N=0. Their positive-index (N+1) count integrals converge respectively to the Gaussian integrals. The corresponding homogeneous entropy, including zero mass, converges to the Gaussian homogeneous entropy. All domains and limits are produced internally.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation reader-main-equation">\[\mu_N=2^{-N}\sum_{\varepsilon\in\{0,1\}^N}\delta_\varepsilon,\quad S_N=N^{-1/2}\sum_j\sigma(\varepsilon_j),\quad\gamma=\mathcal N(0,1);\quad\int A(S_{N+1})\,d\mu_{N+1}\to\int A\,d\gamma\quad(A=f^2,\ f^2\log f^2,\ (f\prime)^2),\quad\operatorname{Ent}_{\mu_{N+1}}(f^2\circ S_{N+1})\to\operatorname{Ent}_{\gamma}(f^2).\]</div><h3>Proof roadmap</h3><ol class="proof-roadmap"><li><span>1</span><strong>Use the actual weak probability laws</strong><p>Invoke the verified actual count-law CLT. Its internally constructed law lambda_N equals the pushforward of the literal count law under the literal sum for everyN. The successor family converges weakly to the exact Gaussian; no caller law or limit certificate enters this theorem.</p></li><li><span>2</span><strong>Build the three bounded compact observers</strong><p>C2 gives continuous f and fprime. Their squares are continuous and compactly supported, since zero is preserved. The map t-&gt;t log t is continuous also at0 and takes0 to0, so f²logf² has the same compact-support property. The derivative support is contained in the support of f.</p></li><li><span>3</span><strong>Produce genuine integrability and count-map transport</strong><p>Each continuous compact observer is genuinely Bochner integrable for every probability law lambda_N and for gamma. The finite sum map is measurable by its finite domain; Integrable.comp_measurable transfers the actual L1 property to the literal count law. The strongly measurable integral-map identity transports the same integrals. L1 is established separately, so totalized integral equalities do not replace domains.</p></li><li><span>4</span><strong>Convert weak convergence to the three real integral limits</strong><p>Root ofCompactSupport packages each actual observer as a bounded continuous function without changing its values. The pinned weak-probability integral characterization gives its Gaussian integral limit. The proven map equality returns the literal successor count integrals.</p></li><li><span>5</span><strong>Combine the homogeneous entropy, including zero mass</strong><p>Let m_N be the actual f² count integral. The mass limit and continuous tlogt give m_N log m_N -&gt; m log m even when m=0. Subtract this limit from the log-observer limit. The separate derivative-observer limit is not the full coordinate-flip-energy limit.</p></li></ol></section><details class="reader-ledger assumption-ledger"><summary>Full assumptions and notation</summary><h3>All objects and hypotheses</h3><ul><li>f:Real-&gt;Real, ContDiff Real 2 f, HasCompactSupport f: exact C2 AND compact support; no normalization or positive mass.</li><li>Canonical real Borel Gaussian of mean0 varianceNNReal1 and canonical finite Boolean carrier. The literal normalized count law and signsum map are fixed; all L1 and limits are outputs.</li><li>Real.log0=0 and tlogt is continuous at0. All N finite L1 includes0; only successor sequences assert asymptotic limits. AtN0 derivative observer equals fprime(0)^2 and need not vanish.</li><li>Authored compact scalar background integration, not printed SPHMC FIRST4.6. Fullflip-energy4, GaussianLSI, finite-Hilbert/noncompact extension, T2, main and expected costs remain open.</li></ul><p class="muted"></p></details><h2>Mathematical proof</h2><div class="proof-reader-step"><h4>1. Use the actual weak probability laws</h4><p>Invoke the verified actual count-law CLT. Its internally constructed law lambda_N equals the pushforward of the literal count law under the literal sum for everyN. The successor family converges weakly to the exact Gaussian; no caller law or limit certificate enters this theorem.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation">\[\lambda_N=(S_N)_\#\mu_N,\qquad\lambda_{N+1}\Rightarrow\gamma.\]</div><details><summary>Corresponding Lean step</summary><p>compact_observer; BalancedRademacherCLT.balanced_count_sum_tendsto_gaussian; hmap</p></details></div><div class="proof-reader-step"><h4>2. Build the three bounded compact observers</h4><p>C2 gives continuous f and fprime. Their squares are continuous and compactly supported, since zero is preserved. The map t-&gt;t log t is continuous also at0 and takes0 to0, so f²logf² has the same compact-support property. The derivative support is contained in the support of f.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation">\[A=f^2,\quad B=A\log A,\quad C=(f\prime)^2,\qquad A,B,C\in C_c(\mathbb R).\]</div><details><summary>Corresponding Lean step</summary><p>hA/sA,hB/sB,hC/sC; ContDiff.continuous_deriv; HasCompactSupport.deriv; HasCompactSupport.comp_left; Real.continuous_mul_log</p></details></div><div class="proof-reader-step"><h4>3. Produce genuine integrability and count-map transport</h4><p>Each continuous compact observer is genuinely Bochner integrable for every probability law lambda_N and for gamma. The finite sum map is measurable by its finite domain; Integrable.comp_measurable transfers the actual L1 property to the literal count law. The strongly measurable integral-map identity transports the same integrals. L1 is established separately, so totalized integral equalities do not replace domains.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation">\[\int g\,d\lambda_N=\int g(S_N)\,d\mu_N,\qquad g\in L^1(\gamma)\cap L^1(\lambda_N),\quad g\circ S_N\in L^1(\mu_N).\]</div><details><summary>Corresponding Lean step</summary><p>compact_observer; hi/hic/hI; Continuous.integrable_of_hasCompactSupport; Integrable.comp_measurable; integral_map_of_stronglyMeasurable</p></details></div><div class="proof-reader-step"><h4>4. Convert weak convergence to the three real integral limits</h4><p>Root ofCompactSupport packages each actual observer as a bounded continuous function without changing its values. The pinned weak-probability integral characterization gives its Gaussian integral limit. The proven map equality returns the literal successor count integrals.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation">\[\int g(S_{N+1})\,d\mu_{N+1}\longrightarrow\int g\,d\gamma\quad(g=A,B,C).\]</div><details><summary>Corresponding Lean step</summary><p>ofCompactSupport; ProbabilityMeasure.tendsto_iff_forall_integral_tendsto; ht; tA/tB/tC</p></details></div><div class="proof-reader-step"><h4>5. Combine the homogeneous entropy, including zero mass</h4><p>Let m_N be the actual f² count integral. The mass limit and continuous tlogt give m_N log m_N -&gt; m log m even when m=0. Subtract this limit from the log-observer limit. The separate derivative-observer limit is not the full coordinate-flip-energy limit.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation">\[\operatorname{Ent}_{\mu_N}(f^2\circ S_N)=\int B(S_N)\,d\mu_N-m_N\log m_N\longrightarrow\int B\,d\gamma-m\log m.\]</div><details><summary>Corresponding Lean step</summary><p>tE; Real.continuous_mul_log.continuousAt.tendsto; Tendsto.comp; Tendsto.sub</p></details></div><section class="lean-verification"><h2>Lean verification</h2><p>The exact proposition and proof begin folded so the mathematical argument remains the primary reading path.</p><details class="inline-lean inline-lean-statement" data-inline-lean="AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.FunctionalInequalities.GaussianCompactEntropy.compact_count_gaussian_entropy_limits"><summary>Lean statement · compact_count_gaussian_entropy_limits</summary><p>For every real C2 function f with compact support, the actual variance-one centered Gaussian integrates f squared, f squared times log(f squared), and the square of its real derivative. Each actual normalized Bool counting measure integrates those same functions of the signed sum divided by sqrt(N), including N=0. Their positive-index (N+1) count integrals converge respectively to the Gaussian integrals. The corresponding homogeneous entropy, including zero mass, converges to the Gaussian homogeneous entropy. All domains and limits are produced internally.</p><p>Braces mark parameters Lean can infer; square brackets request structures such as a measurable space or probability measure. Named hypotheses are mathematical premises, not facts established by this declaration. Section parameters are described in the mathematical hypotheses above; the module link retains their exact source context.</p><pre class="code-block"><code class="language-lean">theorem compact_count_gaussian_entropy_limits
    (f : ℝ → ℝ) (hf : ContDiff ℝ 2 f) (hs : HasCompactSupport f) :
    let μ : (n : ℕ) → Measure (Fin n → Bool) := fun n =&gt;
      (Fintype.card (Fin n → Bool) : ℝ≥0∞)⁻¹ • Measure.count
    let S : (n : ℕ) → (Fin n → Bool) → ℝ := fun n ε =&gt;
      (Real.sqrt (n : ℝ))⁻¹ * ∑ j : Fin n, if ε j then (1 : ℝ) else -1
    let γ : Measure ℝ := gaussianReal 0 1
    Integrable (fun x =&gt; (f x)^2) γ ∧
    Integrable (fun x =&gt; (f x)^2 * Real.log ((f x)^2)) γ ∧
    Integrable (fun x =&gt; (deriv f x)^2) γ ∧
    (∀ n : ℕ,
      Integrable (fun ε =&gt; (f (S n ε))^2) (μ n) ∧
      Integrable (fun ε =&gt; (f (S n ε))^2 * Real.log ((f (S n ε))^2)) (μ n) ∧
      Integrable (fun ε =&gt; (deriv f (S n ε))^2) (μ n)) ∧
    Tendsto (fun n : ℕ =&gt; ∫ ε, (f (S (n+1) ε))^2 ∂μ (n+1)) atTop
      (𝓝 (∫ x, (f x)^2 ∂γ)) ∧
    Tendsto (fun n : ℕ =&gt; ∫ ε,
      (f (S (n+1) ε))^2 * Real.log ((f (S (n+1) ε))^2) ∂μ (n+1)) atTop
      (𝓝 (∫ x, (f x)^2 * Real.log ((f x)^2) ∂γ)) ∧
    Tendsto (fun n : ℕ =&gt; ∫ ε, (deriv f (S (n+1) ε))^2 ∂μ (n+1)) atTop
      (𝓝 (∫ x, (deriv f x)^2 ∂γ)) ∧
    Tendsto (fun n : ℕ =&gt;
      (∫ ε, (f (S (n+1) ε))^2 * Real.log ((f (S (n+1) ε))^2) ∂μ (n+1)) -
      (∫ ε, (f (S (n+1) ε))^2 ∂μ (n+1)) *
        Real.log (∫ ε, (f (S (n+1) ε))^2 ∂μ (n+1))) atTop
      (𝓝 ((∫ x, (f x)^2 * Real.log ((f x)^2) ∂γ) -
        (∫ x, (f x)^2 ∂γ) * Real.log (∫ x, (f x)^2 ∂γ)))</code></pre><p><a href="../modules/autosamplingtheory-technicallemmas-functionalinequalities-gaussiancompactentropy.html#complete-module-source">Exact module and namespace context</a></p></details><details class="inline-lean inline-lean-proof" data-inline-lean="AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.FunctionalInequalities.GaussianCompactEntropy.compact_count_gaussian_entropy_limits"><summary>Lean proof · compact_count_gaussian_entropy_limits</summary><p>Use the actual weak probability laws; Build the three bounded compact observers; Produce genuine integrability and count-map transport; Convert weak convergence to the three real integral limits; Combine the homogeneous entropy, including zero mass</p><p>Braces mark parameters Lean can infer; square brackets request structures such as a measurable space or probability measure. Named hypotheses are mathematical premises, not facts established by this declaration. Section parameters are described in the mathematical hypotheses above; the module link retains their exact source context.</p><pre class="code-block"><code class="language-lean">theorem compact_count_gaussian_entropy_limits
    (f : ℝ → ℝ) (hf : ContDiff ℝ 2 f) (hs : HasCompactSupport f) :
    let μ : (n : ℕ) → Measure (Fin n → Bool) := fun n =&gt;
      (Fintype.card (Fin n → Bool) : ℝ≥0∞)⁻¹ • Measure.count
    let S : (n : ℕ) → (Fin n → Bool) → ℝ := fun n ε =&gt;
      (Real.sqrt (n : ℝ))⁻¹ * ∑ j : Fin n, if ε j then (1 : ℝ) else -1
    let γ : Measure ℝ := gaussianReal 0 1
    Integrable (fun x =&gt; (f x)^2) γ ∧
    Integrable (fun x =&gt; (f x)^2 * Real.log ((f x)^2)) γ ∧
    Integrable (fun x =&gt; (deriv f x)^2) γ ∧
    (∀ n : ℕ,
      Integrable (fun ε =&gt; (f (S n ε))^2) (μ n) ∧
      Integrable (fun ε =&gt; (f (S n ε))^2 * Real.log ((f (S n ε))^2)) (μ n) ∧
      Integrable (fun ε =&gt; (deriv f (S n ε))^2) (μ n)) ∧
    Tendsto (fun n : ℕ =&gt; ∫ ε, (f (S (n+1) ε))^2 ∂μ (n+1)) atTop
      (𝓝 (∫ x, (f x)^2 ∂γ)) ∧
    Tendsto (fun n : ℕ =&gt; ∫ ε,
      (f (S (n+1) ε))^2 * Real.log ((f (S (n+1) ε))^2) ∂μ (n+1)) atTop
      (𝓝 (∫ x, (f x)^2 * Real.log ((f x)^2) ∂γ)) ∧
    Tendsto (fun n : ℕ =&gt; ∫ ε, (deriv f (S (n+1) ε))^2 ∂μ (n+1)) atTop
      (𝓝 (∫ x, (deriv f x)^2 ∂γ)) ∧
    Tendsto (fun n : ℕ =&gt;
      (∫ ε, (f (S (n+1) ε))^2 * Real.log ((f (S (n+1) ε))^2) ∂μ (n+1)) -
      (∫ ε, (f (S (n+1) ε))^2 ∂μ (n+1)) *
        Real.log (∫ ε, (f (S (n+1) ε))^2 ∂μ (n+1))) atTop
      (𝓝 ((∫ x, (f x)^2 * Real.log ((f x)^2) ∂γ) -
        (∫ x, (f x)^2 ∂γ) * Real.log (∫ x, (f x)^2 ∂γ))) := by
  have hA : Continuous (fun x =&gt; (f x)^2) := hf.continuous.pow 2
  have sA : HasCompactSupport (fun x =&gt; (f x)^2) := by
    simpa only [Function.comp_def] using hs.comp_left (g := fun t : ℝ =&gt; t^2) (by simp)
  have hB : Continuous (fun x =&gt; (f x)^2 * Real.log ((f x)^2)) :=
    Real.continuous_mul_log.comp hA
  have sB : HasCompactSupport (fun x =&gt; (f x)^2 * Real.log ((f x)^2)) := by
    simpa only [Function.comp_def] using
      sA.comp_left (g := fun t : ℝ =&gt; t * Real.log t) (by simp)
  have hC : Continuous (fun x =&gt; (deriv f x)^2) :=
    (hf.continuous_deriv (by norm_num)).pow 2
  have sC : HasCompactSupport (fun x =&gt; (deriv f x)^2) := by
    simpa only [Function.comp_def] using
      hs.deriv.comp_left (g := fun t : ℝ =&gt; t^2) (by simp)
  rcases compact_observer (fun x =&gt; (f x)^2) hA sA with ⟨iA, jA, tA⟩
  rcases compact_observer (fun x =&gt; (f x)^2 * Real.log ((f x)^2)) hB sB
    with ⟨iB, jB, tB⟩
  rcases compact_observer (fun x =&gt; (deriv f x)^2) hC sC with ⟨iC, jC, tC⟩
  have tE := tB.sub ((Real.continuous_mul_log.continuousAt.tendsto).comp tA)
  exact ⟨iA, iB, iC, fun n =&gt; ⟨jA n, jB n, jC n⟩, tA, tB, tC, tE⟩

end AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.FunctionalInequalities.GaussianCompactEntropy</code></pre><p><a href="../modules/autosamplingtheory-technicallemmas-functionalinequalities-gaussiancompactentropy.html#complete-module-source">Exact module and namespace context</a></p></details></section><details class="reader-ledger boundary-ledger"><summary>Scope and omitted-condition boundaries</summary><ul><li>Authored compact C2 scalar core: same actual allN Bool count/card/signed sqrt-normalized sum and variance-one Gaussian. Three Gaussian L1 plus allN three actual-count L1 domains and successor mass/log-energy/derivative-square/entropy integral limits are produced internally. No supplied law/domain/limit certificate, normalization or positive mass premise. Fullflip-energy factor4, GaussianLSI, finiteHilbert/noncompact actual sqrtRN cutoff, T2/FIRST4.6/main/work/composition remain open. Focused3162PASS: zero-mass entropy and actual N0 derivative L1/value consumers, three standard3. Independent wholeproof/blind/source/exactcommit and shared publication remain separate.</li></ul></details><details class="proof-reader-provenance reader-ledger"><summary>Sources, dependencies, and reuse</summary><h2>Source and reuse</h2><h3>Samplinglib parents called</h3><ul><li><a href="../theorems/autosamplingtheory-technicallemmas-probability-balancedrademacherclt-balanced-count-sum-tendsto-gaussian.html"><code>AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Probability.BalancedRademacherCLT.balanced_count_sum_tendsto_gaussian</code></a></li></ul><h3>Mathlib API called (external library)</h3><ul><li>MeasureTheory.ProbabilityMeasure.tendsto_iff_forall_integral_tendsto</li><li>ofCompactSupport</li><li>MeasureTheory.Continuous.integrable_of_hasCompactSupport</li><li>MeasureTheory.Integrable.comp_measurable</li><li>MeasureTheory.integral_map_of_stronglyMeasurable</li><li>HasCompactSupport.deriv</li><li>HasCompactSupport.comp_left</li><li>ContDiff.continuous_deriv</li><li>Real.continuous_mul_log</li></ul><h3>Mathematical sources</h3><ul><li><a href="https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06906v1#S4.E6">FIRST S4.E6 GaussianLSI background; SLT GaussianPoincare/Limit.lean compact observer and entropy convergence, including L1213-L1234 actual law-to-entropy use; authored literal Bool-count and rootBCF adapter</a> — Authored compact C2 scalar core: same actual allN Bool count/card/signed sqrt-normalized sum and variance-one Gaussian. Three Gaussian L1 plus allN three actual-count L1 domains and successor mass/log-energy/derivative-square/entropy integral limits are produced internally. No supplied law/domain/limit certificate, normalization or positive mass premise. Fullflip-energy factor4, GaussianLSI, finiteHilbert/noncompact actual sqrtRN cutoff, T2/FIRST4.6/main/work/composition remain open. Focused3162PASS: zero-mass entropy and actual N0 derivative L1/value consumers, three standard3. Independent wholeproof/blind/source/exactcommit and shared publication remain separate.</li><li><a href="https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/blob/db584cd6d46c92f209a44c0f1c829460d327499d/Mathlib/MeasureTheory/Measure/ProbabilityMeasure.lean#L346">Pinned weak-probability integral characterization</a> — Reused compiled Mathlib primitive, no caller weak-law certificate.</li></ul><p>Samplinglib prose is not a quotation or a source-equivalence certificate. Definitions and aliases are explained as constructions, not counted as new mathematical proofs.</p></details></article></main>
